# Copy to git-credentials.docker (git-ignored) and replace the placeholder token
# before running the Docker stack against any private repository (e.g. AgentVault).
#
# Format: one line per host, git's "store" credential-helper format
# (https://git-scm.com/docs/git-credential-store#_storage_format).
#
# Use a GitHub fine-grained personal access token scoped to only the specific
# private repositories that need to be read (e.g. illogical/AgentVault) with
# "Contents: Read-only" repository permission — nothing else. Never use a
# classic token or a broad-scope token here.
#
# This file is bind-mounted read-only into the container at
# /run/secrets/git-credentials (see docker-compose.yml and
# HOMEBASE_HOST_GIT_CREDENTIALS_PATH in .env.docker.example). If you have no
# private repositories configured, point HOMEBASE_HOST_GIT_CREDENTIALS_PATH at
# any existing empty file instead of filling this in.
https://x-access-token:REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_FINE_GRAINED_PAT@github.com
